      "notes": "All claims are well-supported by their cited evidence. Tier assignments are appropriate: parliamentary committee findings are correctly labelled measurable (they are documented facts about committee outputs, not forecasts). The summer 2026 scheme is correctly labelled projected. The E40 quote entails the claim about structural failings without overstatement. The verdict correctly excludes the small-business/procurement elements as economic levers with no direct O9 mechanism. Direction 'improves' at moderate magnitude is defensible given \u00a31.44bn paid to 11,300 claimants alongside documented structural failings. No party-blind issues; the rationale focuses on the due-process deficit and evidence of partial delivery without imputing motive. No false-balance concern: the mixed picture (real progress vs. structural failings) is grounded in claims on both sides. E43 (wsws.org) and E45 (wsws.org) are not used in the verdict claims, avoiding sole reliance on an advocacy/ideological source. Minor observation: the E44 source is listed with source_type 'media' but is gov.uk \u2014 this is a schema-level inconsistency but not a blocking issue for the verdict itself."
